ink that sort of more of the biotech, bioinformatics companies are|||数据分析工作。所以对我来说，这是一个很好的角色，可以让我尝试这两种机会，看看自己喜欢什么。我想多年来，我发现自己其实真的很喜欢软件工程。我发现医疗健康领域的工作对我来说非常有意义且充满动力。我一直想从事对我很重要的事情，以及那些我认为有望让其他人的生活变得更好一点的事情. 所以随着时间的推移，我开始考虑也许我想成为一名软件工程师，但仍然专注于医疗健康领域的某些事情。并且我有兴趣找一家纯软件公司，我觉得它能行动得快一点，就像软件公司那样。我觉得那种生物技术、生物信息学公司往往|||very, very interesting, technically. But sometimes as a software engineer, it could feel a little bit slower since you're sort of only moving at the pace of science, if that makes sense. And, you know, you can't force scientific progress forward and it takes a lot of money to spin up a lab and pass regulations and that type of thing. And so I was looking for somewhere where I could ship software a lot faster, but still make an impact on the healthcare system. Yeah, I think this thing that you mentioned, interesting, is not only found in the healthcare kind of fields or biofields. Like, there's a big difference between working at a place where software is the main product, I guess, and something else is the main product. And I previously had worked somewhere|||在技术上非常非常有趣。但有时作为一名软件工程师，你可能会觉得节奏有点慢，因为你基本上只能以科学的速度前进，如果这说得通的话。而且，你知道的，你无法强行推动科学进步，建立实验室并通过法规等等需要花很多钱。所以我一直在寻找一个地方，在那里我可以更快地发布软件，但仍然对医疗保健系统产生影响。是的，我觉得你提到的这件有趣的事情，不仅在医疗健康领域或生物领域存在。比如，在以软件为主营产品的地方工作，和以其他东西为主营产品的地方工作，这两者之间有很大的区别。我以前曾在某个地方工作过，|||where software was a big part, but not the only part. And then switching to a company where software is the whole part is just a very different approach. I think we need software engineers in both or everywhere, I guess. But yeah, there is this, for I guess, coloring the conversation for people out there thinking about career choices, there really is a difference. I won't say one is better than the other because sometimes when something else is the focus, the sort of cross-function are, are very engaging and entertaining, and even the ability to make a sort of very large difference, because the amount of code being produced, there might be a little bit smaller, so your 